  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Tert-butyl oxide is a strong base and a weak nucleophile.</p><p>In presence of a strong base and heat,&nbsp;elimination reaction favours over substitution reaction.</p><p>The type of elimination taking place here is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>-elimination</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/80b8a7f5-f62d-4586-8b53-817fb298a19b-o5-03-222.png\" style=\"width: 411px; height: 118px;\" />So, option A is the correct answer.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
